WEBVTT

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:09.730
Huh?!

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.730
George Beresford...?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.700
Yeah, do you remember him?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.070
How could I forget someone so annoying?

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.620
His company, Bad Dwarf, is doing a
competition for unpublished games soon.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.160
Good games have a chance
to get published, but...

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.540
Why are you telling me this?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.300
Well, he called me the other day.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.330
Yes, send a message to
that fledgling designer for me:

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.140
I haven't played your game yet.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.560
Haven't played yet...

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:54.520
So he's challenging me to show him my game.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.740
Oh, um, I mean, it's totally up
to you whether you want to join.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.110
School starts tomorrow. You won't
have any time to make games, right?

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:38.960
What?!

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.920
You're participating in a competition?

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.200
Yes.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.470
What exactly is a competition?

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:51.120
In this case, competition means that
they're accepting game submissions

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.020
and will choose which game is best.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.450
Sort of like a contest, I guess.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.450
I see!

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:00.480
That's impressive! Which competition is this?

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.040
The one by Bad Dwarf, in the US.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.650
Oh! Bad Dwarf!

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:09.660
But there will be professional authors
in that competition, too, right?

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.580
Of course, I don't think I have a chance to win.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.750
Maybe they'll completely ignore me.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.250
But at any rate, I decided
not to run away from this.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.920
No matter how it ends.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.880
Midori-chan...

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:27.160
So... I was hoping to ask you
three to help me test the game.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.390
Can you help me...?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.580
You don't have to ask!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.890
Yes, I'm looking forward to Midori's game!

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.370
<i>One Room</i>, version two.
The game system was improved overall.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.450
Wow...

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.530
It looks more game-like than before!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.750
These cards are furniture.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.320
Yes. The goal of the game is
to collect furniture for your room.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.620
First, you deal ten cards
from the top of the deck...

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.210
...and that's the basic flow.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.910
Emmy, do you get it?

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.330
Yes, I understand!

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:07.170
You work to make money
and buy furniture for your room.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.000
Furniture items have points,
and bonuses are given

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.330
by getting same-colored
furniture or by completing a set.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:22.450
Yes. The big difference from the first version
is that there are more ways to score points.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.530
Of course, getting expensive furniture
is a good way to score a lot of points.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:30.540
There are more furniture types than before!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.870
And we have pets now, too!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.740
The work schedule is a chart now, too.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.120
Yeah, I figured fixing the values might
help make the choices more difficult.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:48.080
I see... This forces you to strategize
on when to buy and when to save up.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.920
Good thinking, Midori-chan.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.550
Yes, I made a lot of adjustments.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.770
The basic flow is the same, but I see
that it's evolved a lot from before.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:01.480
This looks like lots of fun!
Let's play right away!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.110
Okay, time to give it a try!

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.520
Yes!

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.910
Okay, we've all placed our workers.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:16.950
Me first! I got paid, so I'll buy this table!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.210
Well, I'll buy this sofa then.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.450
I'll take seven gold and pass.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.290
That's the end of round one.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.680
And finally, add up the bonus points...

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:45.150
Aya, 92 points. Emmy, 84 points.
Miki, 84 points. Manager, 79 points.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.910
So... that's the game. What do you think?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:55.040
Incredible, Midori-chan!
This is totally a proper game!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.700
Yes, it's much more fun than before!

00:05:58.700 --> 00:05:59.990
How about you, Emmy?

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.580
Yes, it's a very cleanly designed game,
very much like Midori herself.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.540
It's super, super great, Midori-chan!

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.040
You'll make it in the
competition, too, for sure!

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.500
Midori-chan?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.370
What do you think, Manager?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.180
Yes, I am surprised.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:21.560
When I first tried it, it was full of holes.
The improvement is huge.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:23.680
But...

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.650
...it probably still isn't going
to get far in the competition.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.820
This game is too neatly put together,
for better and for worse.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:38.750
What?! Manager, what do you mean?!
This game can't compete?!

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.870
It's okay, Aya.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.830
Midori-chan... But...

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:42.870
It's fine.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:47.380
I also felt there was something off
while I was making it.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:52.590
Like the manager said, this game
is still missing something crucial.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.830
Midori-chan...

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.050
That said, there's no need to rush this.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:03.020
You're still a first-year high school
student. You've come quite far.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.790
Don't worry about the competition.
Just take your time and--

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:06.980
No, I can't do that!

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.230
What?!

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:13.120
That would mean I ran away again...

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.750
Ran away from him...

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.820
Don't overthink this.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.370
Emmy...?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:27.460
When I make games, I also run into moments
where it doesn't come out as imagined.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.340
When that happens, I think in simple terms.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.080
Simple...

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.300
Yes! Just do all the things you want to do!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.500
All of the things I want to do...?

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:47.310
Huh? What did I originally want
to accomplish by making this game...?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.020
What...?

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.280
The showroom for the furniture
company that my dad owns...

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.950
It has been my favorite place
since I was very small.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.990
Miss Midori!

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:04.370
Sakamoto.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.000
Are you alone? Is your father with you?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.710
No, and it doesn't matter
whether he's here or not.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:13.330
Oh, you must have had a disagreement again.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:17.830
In that case, allow me
to cast a fun spell on you.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.750
A spell? How old do you think I am?

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.510
I'm not a child anymore.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:28.910
Please, indulge me. Give this a try.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.440
I have one just like this at home...

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.080
How does it feel?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.860
It's... not bad.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:45.030
I am glad that it suits you.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.210
Sakamoto's recommendations are flawless.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:51.700
Dad always brags about how

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:56.410
you're the best floor master and
interior coordinator in the industry.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.800
I am unworthy of such kind words.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:03.120
Don't be modest. Is this a new sofa?

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.870
Yes, it is from Germany.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.500
What is striking about this piece is how,

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.200
in pursuit of functional perfection,
it has arrived at a bold new aesthetic--

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.700
Sakamoto, you really love furniture, don't you?

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.280
Yes, I find it is my true calling.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.910
Such an exaggeration.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.990
Oh, no, I am not exaggerating.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:31.500
No matter how much one loves furniture,
there's only so much a person can buy.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:37.460
But in this profession, I can lay out all
of this furniture in any way I please.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:41.920
It is a luxury no ordinary person can enjoy.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:47.640
Therefore, my work is,
without a doubt, what I live for.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.040
What you live for...?

00:09:56.750 --> 00:10:00.900
All of the furniture here were picked
by my dad according to his tastes.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.860
If I could choose for myself...

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:07.950
...I'd choose this desk... and this chair!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.000
This chair is 270,000 yen?!

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.750
And the desk...

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.960
450,000 yen?!

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:22.160
Wow, I never knew good
furniture could be this expensive.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:25.120
I grew up around them
without even thinking about it.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.550
Sakamoto is right.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:35.060
But... if I could, one day,
put any furniture I want, wherever I want...

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:39.110
...that would really
be a luxury, right, Sakamoto?

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.830
Place furniture freely...

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:46.530
Oh!

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:48.700
Wh-What is it, Midori-chan?!

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.240
You startled me...

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.040
That's it... How did I forget?

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.080
The thing I really wanted to do.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:03.210
This game is only half done at this point.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:22.950
If the remainder is 13x minus 5,
what is the value of A?

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.440
Seriously?

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:23.650
Midori-chan is completely asleep?

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.320
So who can answer this question...?

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.150
Ono?

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:34.200
A equals open parentheses 4x cubed
minus x squared plus 4x squared

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:37.790
minus x minus 12x plus 3 close parentheses

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:43.750
plus 13x minus 5 equals 4x cubed
plus 3x squared minus 2.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.050
Good, correct.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:49.550
Whoa! Nice, Ono! Impressive...

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.950
Midori is behaving weirdly?

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.400
Yeah, Emmy!

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:13.740
She won't play with us at all,
always looks sleepy and distant...

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.330
Lots of things are weird about her!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.410
That's not the Midori-chan we know!

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.380
It's okay.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:24.710
Let's give her some space for now.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.130
She should bring us a really fun game soon.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.850
I have been awaiting your arrival, Miss Midori.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:40.500
Sorry to bother you during
work hours, Sakamoto.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.230
I just needed a few more photos...

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:45.830
Miss Midori?!

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.700
Are you all right?

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.830
I'm fine, I just tripped on myself.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:56.580
I hate to be presumptuous,
but are you getting enough sleep lately?

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.960
You look unwell...

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.790
I might not have slept for a couple of days.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.200
Miss Midori!

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:07.370
I'm fine. I feel sharper than ever.

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:09.290
But...

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.500
Hey, Sakamoto.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:11.300
Yes...?

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:15.890
You once said that furniture
is what you live for, right?

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:20.180
I used to think you were
exaggerating, but now I understand.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.940
I found one, too--a "thing to live for."

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.570
Somewhere in my mind,
I was trapped into thinking

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.740
that a professional's game
should be a certain way.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.830
Because of that, I left my own
desires out of the equation.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:45.170
Emmy is right. This is my game.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:50.050
I'm allowed to pack it full
of the things I want to do!

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.600
Is Midori-chan okay?

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.950
She's been out with a cold for three days...

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.200
And she's been behaving weirdly.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.830
I... I'm going to go see Midori-chan!

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.700
I'm coming, too!

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.790
Both of you, calm down.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:10.570
Let's all visit her together.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.110
The snow is heavy this year...

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.410
Oh, good, you're all here.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:27.700
What are you doing, Aya?

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.500
Midori-chan, you idiot!
What were you doing?!

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.160
A-Aya?

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.450
Midori-chan, are you okay now?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:36.470
Miki...

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.540
I'm sorry, I might have lost sight
of my surroundings for a bit.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.000
My cold is better now, too, so...

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.690
It seems like you've finished it, Midori.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.150
Yes, finally.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:54.150
Finished? You mean...

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.490
Furniture tokens! So cute!

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:01.740
Did you make all of these yourself?!

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:04.660
Yes, based on some photos I took.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:07.580
It must have been a lot
of work to make so many.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:10.960
Seriously, a lot. So we choose from here?

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:14.880
Yes, this is the shop.
It's a bit awkward looking, but...

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.300
And, here.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.660
Ah! This board is a room!

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:27.480
And you buy furniture from the shop board
and put it on your room board.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.070
By buying more furniture...

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:35.190
Wow! You can really build a room!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:40.370
A game where you can choose the furniture
that you like to make a unique room.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:45.620
That's the original intent of the game
when I first decided to make it.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:47.870
What do you think?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.120
This looks like lots of fun!

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:53.500
Yes! The boards, the tokens, they're all great.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.840
Midori-chan! Let's play!

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.260
Really? Okay...

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.470
The basic flow is the same as before.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:08.850
On your turn, place your marker and
determine your income and purchase order.

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:10.190
Next is shopping.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.160
What is this black piece?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.480
That is an existing customer.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.950
You can't shop in a store that
already has a customer in it.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:24.740
The black piece moves every round,
so you have to time your shopping correctly.

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:28.250
So if you can't shop in a store
that already has a customer...

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:33.000
Yes, so naturally, you can't go into
the same store as another player.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.920
I knew it...

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.700
So you need to make the first move
in order to get what you want...

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.630
It's a shopping race!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:46.790
This time, if someone purchases
ten items, the game is over.

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:51.100
By the way, the person who buys
ten items gets a ten point bonus!

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:55.320
Now that there are so many choices,
it's hard to decide where to start...

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:57.910
That's why I came up with these.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.040
Hmm? What is it?

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.280
Catalog cards.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:08.750
If you can get all the items written on
the card, you get a bonus added to your score.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:12.210
These cards must have
been tough to make, Midori.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:16.830
Can you tell?! Just by looking at it?!
I knew you'd get it, Emmy!

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:20.200
Yes, making the adjustments on
those cards was the hardest part.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.580
I see...

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.930
Midori-chan and Emmy
understand each other quite well.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.430
Time to play-test!

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.330
Let's start!

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:33.020
Yeah!

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:41.530
Okay, me first.
I get six gold and buy this rug...

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:45.620
It's like the time I moved here!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:49.830
I had no furniture so my room was huge!

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.620
Okay, I choose this sofa.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.950
Oh, that sofa is cute!

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.790
An Asian style!

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:02.260
Midori and I just get money and pass.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.250
Neither of you are shopping?

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:10.080
No. Saving money to buy expensive
furniture gets you more points.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.180
Huh?!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:12.950
She's right...!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.400
I didn't notice...

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:18.290
Wait, this cabinet is 14 points?!

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.110
I... I have to save...

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:23.370
Calm down, both of you.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.910
Buying expensive furniture is risky, too.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:26.950
Risky?

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:31.790
Yes. This game is over
when someone buys ten things.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.330
In other words...

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:37.290
I see, if the game ends
while you're saving up...

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:40.000
Yes, that would be disastrous.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:46.470
And there's that ten point bonus for
having the largest amount of furniture...

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:50.930
I get it! So you could try to just buy
a lot of cheap stuff to win early...

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:52.580
Could work.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:54.750
Oh, but there's also the catalog cards...

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.400
Oh, that bonus, too!

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:00.290
We'd need to get these bonuses, too,
in order to win, right?

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.690
Wait, so I have to save money after all!

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:05.570
Start off by getting the
items on the catalogs, and...

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.120
Would I have time to save money...?

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.120
They're all strategizing...

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:09.410
What if I want the same
things as the others...?

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.740
They're totally engrossed in my game!

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:10.700
What if I want the same
things as the others...?

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.330
I already know what I want to buy!

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.500
I'm so glad...

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.500
Hmm, what to do...

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:19.380
I'm so incredibly happy right now!

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.200
Game over!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:27.660
I couldn't get the cabinet after all!

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:29.640
Let's add up the bonuses...

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:37.980
Miki, 82 points. Emmy, 84 points.
Aya, 84 as well. I got 92 points...

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.830
What?! You won by a huge margin? Not fair!

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:45.900
I can't help it. I made this game, so...

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.750
Wh-What?

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:49.620
Oh, right...

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:50.450
Yes!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:53.120
Midori-chan made this game!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:56.790
That totally slipped our minds,
we were so engrossed in the game.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:00.000
S-Stop flattering me...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.960
This is not flattery, Midori.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:06.220
There are many different
choices and lots of freedom.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.250
This is truly a good game.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:12.040
Yes, there are so many more ways to
play than the previous version. It's fun!

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:16.180
Yeah, it's awesome that
you made this all by yourself!

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:17.810
By myself...?

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:20.980
No, that's not it.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.580
I couldn't have made this game alone.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.360
Huh?

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.820
It's all thanks to you. Thank you very much.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.410
That's not true... Right?

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:37.450
We didn't know you were
working on this while you were out...

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:41.290
Yeah. We didn't help at all...

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:44.640
What are you talking about?
You played with me!

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.700
But that's normal--

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:50.470
Those normal things
are exactly what I needed!

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:55.680
Without someone to play with,
I wouldn't have been able to move forward.

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:57.500
Midori-chan...

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.310
Someone said, a while ago,

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:06.500
the game would never be completed
as long as I thought about it by myself.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:09.530
At the time, I was just mad
at him and snapped back, but...

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:13.370
I think I understand what he meant now.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.490
Who is he?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:24.290
George Beresford. Making him play my game
is one of my goals for this competition.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:28.330
Beresford...? The designer at Bad Dwarf?

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.330
You know him, Midori?

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:35.620
He's an old friend of the manager. He's an
annoying and stubborn old man, though.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:39.520
Your dream is ahead of mine,
Midori. I'm impressed!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:44.560
No, it was only with your help that
I was able to see what I really wanted.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.230
It's you who is ahead of me.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:48.480
Midori...

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:52.540
You both have great dreams, it's so cool!

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:53.790
Don't you think so, Miki-chan?

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.910
Y-Yeah, I think so, too.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:59.250
What is this feeling...?

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:02.410
I'm happy for her, but also a little...

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:03.540
...sad?

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:39.430
This past year was lots of fun.

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:45.850
But am I the only one who
wants to stay this way forever?
